    <type2:TagsetDescription xmi:id="1420481" sofa="1" begin="0" end="0" layer="webanno.custom.Sentences_Separation" name="Sentences_Separation" input="false"/>
    <cas:Sofa xmi:id="1" sofaNum="1" sofaID="_InitialView" mimeType="text" sofaString="Tutorial classes helped me to understand the lessons properly, with the examples.&#13;&#10;The lecture is clear and understandable . but the person who know nothing in java could trouble at start. So If he tutorial class is conducted from the beginning it would be better. It's pleasure studying in your lecture. Thank you. &#13;&#10;It was overall a great series of lectures. We were able to learn a lot of new things. Thanks for having tutorial classes and doing more examples. It helped us a lot. We expect Dr. Marcia to take the whole lectures.  &#13;&#10;Providing better understanding of objected oriented programming. Able to make better structured programs. Helps to improve coding quality.&#13;&#10;teaching approaches are good. but this subject is very hard to me. I don't know that how do i work with it. I have interest in this subject. we want tutorial also. thank you.&#13;&#10;Give lab not only for semi project bt some exercises specially in threada and event handling... give some sample coding to fill.. and give a startup cls in the begining apart from oop for java language&#13;&#10;Dear Madam,    You taught well through out the semester 2. Thank you for initilizing tutorial class and doing extra questions. By doing questions as assessments within the class we can keep our memory regarding subject easily.&#13;&#10;Your lectures were very good and also the tutorial was help us to write answers&#13;&#10;Lectures were interesting.   Was able to understand the basics of OOP.    suggestion - a way to cover basic java for students who don't know java.    Thanks. :)&#13;&#10;The best thing i saw is that we could ask questions during the class and clear out our problems.   Tutorial classes was much helpful.&#13;&#10;Overall learning outcome is satisfactory.&#13;&#10;Need more additional excercise&#13;&#10;Thanks for thinking from our side always. It is a big help to have project evaluation after the exam&#13;&#10;Lectures were good enough to understand  explanations were good.  Examples were adequate but there might be some more excersises too  &#13;&#10;friendly lecturer.  Help us in any question.  overall teaching can be recommended as good.  but practicals are not well organized&#13;&#10;Actually course was really good and well planned. tutorial classes were really beneficial and if motivated do do past papers.thank you!&#13;&#10;Good.Better if more descriptive sample codes are given and explained. Tutorials were really helpful.&#13;&#10;The course was done in a proper manner. Tutorials are useful. I was able to understand the fundamentals of OOP.&#13;&#10;Well structered lectures  But we want some more code practice.&#13;&#10;Tutorials which conducted by you were very helpful..so we had a proper idea how to answer questions in the paper and got a wide and clear idea about the subject matter while answering the practical related questions....&#13;&#10;We got more advantages from the tutorial classes. But I think the Lab sessions were not used efficiently. If every lab session had a submission of semester project it could be useful.&#13;&#10;Great. Could improve by adding by adding debugging methods as a subject section.&#13;&#10;introducing tutorials was great   :-) .i really participated in each and every tutorial and participated all of the lectures because lecture series were so efficient and interesting. madame i think it would have been better if regular tasks were given in the labs instead of carrying a single project throughout the semester.&#13;&#10;Lectures was well structured to target the necessary theory parts. it helps to understand easily. Well describe the theories at the lectures. Specially tutorial classes helps to understand the facts through the problems. I think tutorials will help to the end exam also.I think it is better to continue these ways to this module in future also and wish to do so in future.&#13;&#10;I really liked the course. After the mid semester I found it difficult to code what had been taught (as I have no previous knowledge in coding in Java).     Madam, I suggest it would have been better if you give more in class exercises with practical scenarios earlier rather than doing it at the end. The in class exercises help a lot in understanding the theory plus coding it.&#13;&#10;Very well prepared&#13;&#10;The lectures were well structured and informative. The approaches to instill the concepts in us were really good. The viva for the mid-evaluation was a good experience.&#13;&#10;The lectures and labs were well organized in the whole lecture series. Madam, you tried to do more examples even arranging a tutorial class and it was very useful to us. It's better if you can do some more questions taking a part of the time reserved to lab sessions.&#13;&#10;The lectures and examples done were clear. Applying threads is confusing. More examples on threads would have been better.&#13;&#10;conducted lectures were well managed and understandable.   I have learned valuable educational things.   Thank u.&#13;&#10;All the lectures were well organized and great. Examples and homework questions are good and motivating.&#13;&#10;Overall content is pretty good. Lectures were comprehensive. It would have been better if more tutorial classes were arranged.&#13;&#10;lecture series is sufficient for get understand about OOP priniples. Basic concepts you taught are good. But thread and observer observable design is not good enough like those. I think it will good if we are given more code example with sufficint description for make understand the coding practice.&#13;&#10;Lecture slides were easy to understand.  Tutorial class is very useful to me.  Pastpaper and examples help to understand theory. Overall this course is good to me.&#13;&#10;All the lecture series were understandable and many questions were discussed during the class.The tutorial class really helped to solve our problems in implementing concepts that taught in the class room.  Discussing past papers during the tutorial class was really helped to get an idea about the paper and also the course.We felt free to ask question during the class time and we were able solve our questions in the class room.  So we were able to finish the course successfully.&#13;&#10;the lecturer is very friendly and very enthusiastic to answer question. She put extra classes n order to help us to understand things more clearly. Pleasure to have a such lecturer.&#13;&#10;Module was confident to learn about oop as all lectures were well structured and well organized. In class exercises were also useful to learn the module. Tutorial class is more valuable than them because it is easy to understand theories after doing self-studies. I can ensure that I got a clear knowledge about poop and how to apply them in practically.&#13;&#10;very good lecture series.  madam could you please upload the 2014 OOP exam paper.&#13;&#10;Lectures and tutorial class is very good and very helpful. It will be a really good help if tutorial class conducts tommorow&#13;&#10;Course was great. Work load is acceptable. Continuos assesment tested my abilities well. I got Madam Marcia for my mid evaluation. Although I got low marks, it helped me to improve my ability, understanding my mistakes.&#13;&#10;I'm really appreciate your dedications to teach this module from the start of this semester. Also we gained a great improvements through the tutorial classes. And I don't have any complaints regarding this module. Thank you.&#13;&#10;good..&#13;&#10;The lecture slides and the teachings were clear and well organized and helped me to understand the necessary learning outcomes. the tutorials were important because it was a chance to understand how we should answer the questions. wish there was a separate time slot from the very beginning.&#13;&#10;Lectures are well structured, so we can   catch points of the lesson easily. But sometimes teaching speed was very high.   But overall lecturing pattern was satisfactory.&#13;&#10;Course is very useful. Helped to gain the knowledge from the basic concepts..&#13;&#10;This module was well organized and helped us to learn opp concepts very clearly.Discussing past papers within the class helped us to learn the pattern of answering the questions,moreover the tutorial classes were really important and it is better have more tutorial classes.&#13;&#10;I believe that the expected outcomes of the course was achieved. Dr. Marcia was punctual and conducted the lecture sessions in a more exciting manner. All of the lecture slides were posted on the moodle which was helpful   .It wouldn't have been in vain if Dr.Marcia had done more examples in class though. Although the slides were posted on the moodle, I had a hard time following them. IMO they were not descriptive enough.    The help of the instructors at the lab sessions substantially improved my approach towards java and programming.    Overall, this was a module I enjoyed following.&#13;&#10;I have a good impression about how the course is conducted.&#13;&#10;Tutorial classes were helped us to get more knowledge about this module.&#13;&#10;I learnt a lot of things during the lecture series and also lecture slides were very useful. I sincerely grateful about the tutorial also...&#13;&#10;It is difficult to understand threads and event handling.&#13;&#10;Madam,   Lecture Explanations are very good and enough, Can you explain about the semi exam paper model? we want a coding exercise.  &#13;&#10;The course is really good.  But I feel that it would be better if we can have a java class running parallel.  The lecturers commitment can be clearly seen and should be appriciated.&#13;&#10;Tutorial is good to develop answering to papers.&#13;&#10;Course was good.   Good idea to evaluate the game after the exam because then we can give more time to develop it.  Tutorial classes were very helpful.  Some times I felt details were less in lecture slides.&#13;&#10;Extra classes were very helpful.  Semester project was really helpful to understand the practical use of OOP concepts.Since there was no GUI included , there were no confusions.Out of three OOP projects I have done this one was the most helpful and the most clear.I am so glad I took this subject this semester, because I think I obtained   a good knowledge on OOP as well as JAVA.I am really glad since I was able to complete the project on my own and I am very confident now because of that.Looking forward to OOSD course.Dear madam,thank you very much for your support.  -Alice  &#13;&#10;I think the lecture series was great. There is no much to change. Tutorial class was extremely helpful. I learned a lot from tutorial class. Thank you for conducting the tutorial class spending your valuable time madam. It was a great pleasure learning from you.&#13;&#10;Additional class to do more coding helped us a lot. I think that time should be more than 1 hour. If not it would be better at least if you could post sample answers for few problems like that so we could check answers ourselves and correct our faults.   However I think the lecture series went well.   Thank you..!!&#13;&#10;Lectures were well planned and explained the OOP concepts using real world examples. Mid examination and the viva helped me to check my knowledge in OOP. The examples discussed in tutorial classes were very useful to get an understanding about the concepts and to practice writing codes. The lecturs were kind of discussions among students and students were free to ask questions about the subject&#13;&#10;Lectures and tutorial class were very useful to improve our knowladge on object oriented concepts.&#13;&#10;More examples should have been done on threads to explain the whole section. The explainations given in other sections were sufficient.&#13;&#10;great.  more examples will be more helpful&#13;&#10;Tutorial classed in which we discussed past exam papers and modal questions were really helpful.&#13;&#10;Those lectures were very helpful to improve my OOP knowledge.&#13;&#10;lectures are good. well organized. with in class tests it is easy to understand things.&#13;&#10;If we given the answer code in java.It will be useful for us to compare with our code and we will be able to notice our mistakes.&#13;&#10;It was fruitful in enhancing the programming concepts in our minds.  In class activities were the most effective ones.&#13;&#10;Good. Specially the homework exercises done were really helpful in grasping the concepts of OOP.&#13;&#10;All the necessary principles are discussed well.&#13;&#10;They gave a good introduction to the concepts of object oriented programming but perhaps when they should be used and more importantly when they should not be used could had been explained more indepth&#13;&#10;Overall, the lectures were good. In class activities hleped a lot. But some key points were only mentioned in passing in the lectures, a written summary of the section finished would be helpful in the future. It is really impressive to see how much you value student feedback :)&#13;&#10;All seven lectures were good for me.  But, I think there are some people don't know java. Onething would be helpful to them that you might tell section or topic in java what you were going to do in next lectures. All of the lectures were awesome. But madam, I am afraid of exam that there are essay type questions in past final examinations. I understood everything you taught in the subject. But, I don't have plenty of words to describe that since I haven't done them yet. Madam, do I need to write exactly what you taught or can I write it using some of my own words?  Home and I class activities would be helpful to everybody if they have done it themselves. Semester project also helped me to experience programming principles while going through it.&#13;&#10;It was great! In class activities were very useful to understand the principles and theories&#13;&#10;Concepts are taught step by step.It was good..  In Classe activities are used to understand the concepts..  &#13;&#10;It is very useful. please put tutorial class for weak students like as me.&#13;&#10;all the lectures were good.  reminding the last week lecture briefly was best.  doing examples for each concept was helpful.  &#13;&#10;anonymous is the inner class in java,it has no name.&#13;&#10;All the lectures were pretty good  Understood many hard points  It would be great if there was some coding representations too  &#13;&#10;shortly they are good enough for me..&#13;&#10;Thank you for your lectures.  It will be help us to under stand OOP concept and learning Java language. thankyou&#13;&#10;I understood most of what was being taught with regard to OOP concepts but the unfamiliarity with the programming language hindered understanding the implementation of the concepts.     Also, making the semester project the first introduction into Java was confusing. If simplper problems like the coffee shop were introduced first, where we could run the code and find out the results, it would have been better.&#13;&#10;Really good lectures but without having knowledge of java no one can understand so next year onwards please tell the students to learn the java befor start studying&#13;&#10;UML lecture was litte bit speed.so didn't get clear understand about the lesson.  lectures about OOP concepts fine.&#13;&#10;Lectures were well organized. It is more useful if there were another some example codes in classroom.&#13;&#10;I think the class activities and lab activities are good.&#13;&#10;Lectures were well constructed and very clear to understand. Activities helped me to understand unclear parts.     Please add the answer code or an example code with moodlle HomeWork activities. It will help us to follow the coding standards and correct coding methods. So we can improve our coding style. And Please add lecture slides to moodle day before the lecture.It will help us to get an idea about the next lecture.        &#13;&#10;Lectures were fully organized and carried out as organized. Some students including me, don't revise before coming to next lectures. Still it was capable to understand it as a quick review is made on previous lectures.&#13;&#10;I think it's better to discuss more java codes for small parts rather than discussing big examples in the class.&#13;&#10;Revising the previous week's lesson is effective.   in-class exercises and homework also provide a way to identify our weak points and improve.   &#13;&#10;good.had a better knowledge on oop  &#13;&#10;we could understand oop theory by in-class activity discussion.In class activities were very important to implement the semester project reducing cohesion and coupling.some lectures were fast.but it could understand from problems.&#13;&#10;It helped us to learn, that previous week's lesson was revised each lecture.   It was bit difficult to follow in the beginning because it was a completely new subject but now we can follow the lecture.&#13;&#10;Due to the nature of the module it might be necessary to give conceptual scenarios like BicycleFactories, BeverageMachines.   But it would be clearer if we a more specific programming task that involves OOP is given.     For example instead of BeverageMachine (which doesn't do any actual work inside the code but rather deals with concepts like Tea,Coffee) I recommend something like a MathBot (which takes some real input do some real process and produces an output, but of course it might be hard to incorporate OOP into this)&#13;&#10;It would have been better if the lecturer taught bit slower because some parts were hard to grab. Other than that everything was fine.&#13;&#10;oop lectures were very good and one suggestion which felt, will help to increase the understanding of concepts of oop. dicussing more than one example of code for a given topic or reference links to such examples will help us to understand the subject better.&#13;&#10;Understandable. I did not know java when I was coming to the university and now i can manage java to some extend. Lectures were started from the beginning of the language not from the scratch but however it was manageable because that is around the starting point.&#13;&#10;until lecture of Abstraction it was easy to understand and after that from polymorphysim it was little hard to understand the theory.but since we had in class activities and various activities in lab session we could be able to understand that.    if we can have the answers of in class activities and lab activities after that week it will be more help to us to identify our weaknesses and improve our skill.&#13;&#10;Thanks for last two homework answers. It is easy to understand java oop concept. Every homework activity you give answer that is easy to our studies. This is my opinion. If you teach small slow we understand easy. I learn everything.&#13;&#10;The lectures were really good but sometimes, they were fast and was hard to capture the matters discussed. The lecture on polymorphism was not much understandable. The rest were really good&#13;&#10;This 7 lectures was helpful to learn more.In class activities were more helpful to understand.I could understand the concept of oop well.Thank you.&#13;&#10;it was good. lecturer tried many ways to interact with student. if we many more exercises, it will be useful. i think conducting tutorial will be useful in future&#13;&#10;Oop concepts are teached by her very well. I understood them and the homeworks and other activities done by her motivate us for the subject&#13;&#10;Lectures were good! but it's better if the presentation slides were more descriptive.Some codes discussed in the lectures were some kind of difficult to understand since the time it was given was not enough.(since most of us are still learning to code in java).  -------  Kindly request madam to conduct a tutorial class weekly hoping it would be very significant to those who are week in Oop concepts.    Thank you.&#13;&#10;All lectures are very difficulty to understand.   But in practical time we can understand its.  In class activities are very helpful.  &#13;&#10;Every lecture was very useful. in-class exercises was really helpful. If the discussion is done for every in class exercise or if the answers are uploaded to the moodle, it will be more helpful.       If possible please conduct tutorials.&#13;&#10;all the 7 lectures were very helpful for me. Since i had not very big knowledge about JAVA, all the things dicussed at class , activities done at class were helpful to understand the concepts&#13;&#10;The lectures were good and very useful.&#13;&#10;Lecturer explained the concepts well and used comparisons with real world scenarios which are helpful to understand the meaning behind the concepts. Lecturer also asked questions from the class and welcomed questions by students as well which was good. The more use of images in examples might help the beginners to understand better. Also, more information regarding the semester project being given at the beginning would be preferable (how it's supposed to run etc...)&#13;&#10;Very good..we had a big knowledge  &#13;&#10;Lectures are understandable but little confusing whether we have to use all those practices if we can write the code in a different but easier manner ....Group exercises we did on the earlier lectures were really good because we could actively participate on the lecture....I wish madam, you could do more of those&#13;&#10;it has helped me to get good of knowledge about oop basic concepts.&#13;&#10;It's better if we receive printed handouts for important oop concepts.  Evaluate each week of code rather than waiting till end of semester by homework .  &#13;&#10;They are well conducted and I got learned basic concepts of OOP clearly.&#13;&#10;concepts of oop was done well but last lecture about uml diagrams was bit confusing. And it would be nice if more questions were discussed in the class.&#13;&#10;First four lectures was easy to understand and the concepts were taught in a excellent manner by doing in class activities.Continuing the semester project and doing in class activities,as the concepts are taught helped me to understand the points that I struggle with.In talking about teaching style lecturer's teaching style is excellent but in terms of improvement it will be more better if the examples are explained slowly and precisely.honestly, I learn the most through examples.In addition to that lecture five six was difficult for me to understand.In lecture 6 there wasn't enough examples describing A\association.I would be grateful if is explained again in a tutorial class.Lecture 7 was regarding an in class activity.Through that lecture I was quite able to understand UML diagrams.&#13;&#10;I really liked how lecture used a lot of examples so that concepts were more easily understood.but the major throwback was the lack of Java knowledge to clearly understand some points,(as a example runnble interface was used but didn't have much idea about it).&#13;&#10;It was definitely useful. In-class activities and homework were helpful to grasp somewhat new concepts of OOP.&#13;&#10;Doing many example problems in class is very good.    Displaying and correcting randomly selected code parts of our submitted codes are also good. We sometimes find the same mistake in our codes too.        &#13;&#10;It is very helpful!!!!  Thank madam.&#13;&#10;give more examples to understand the oop concepts.  white board is not clear. use dark colour marker.  provide soft copy sample codes to understand the concepts&#13;&#10;All concepts can be easily understood because of the examples.&#13;&#10;&gt; We were taught OOP concepts in first few lectures, but I could not understand the mechanism to use those concepts.    &gt;After doing some example questions, my problem was solved.    &gt;Therefore, if you can do small example questions(with explaining codes) in first few lectures it will be helpful for those who are struggling with java.    &gt;Furthermore, if you can show codes while explaining, it is better than writing codes on the board.&#13;&#10;How you did the lectures was good madam.But Encapsulation and other lectures after that lectures were little bit some difficulties to understand.You tried hard to give your knowledge to us.You made tutorial classes,home works.We appreciate that madam and thanks for the effort you did.&#13;&#10;The lectures were well organized. Introduced the concepts step by step in a clear manner. In class activities helped to clear out doubts if there were any. Very much satisfied with the lectures.&#13;&#10;The order of the lecture was vary use full to us. Example code was not enough more code will give clear idea.&#13;&#10;Thank you for having good lectures.We find it useful.If really student concentrate on what is being taught he should have at least 70% subject matters covered.In class exercises are useful and the way that labs are assigned help us to practice what we have studied......Thanks for the lone tutorials.Please make sure in future though tutorials are need not to be mandatory,but some will find them useful.Really some students learn from doing questions..........&#13;&#10;It is very essential for us because it gave us so many unknown things about java .&#13;&#10;At beginning I did not know anything about Java. So the first few lectures was hard for me. But your explanations on OOP were very clear and simple. Therefore after few practicals it was normal. Then I was not able to attend some lectures and now I have some problems. Otherwise your teaching methods and in class activities was so efficient and helped so much.  thank you madam,&#13;&#10;It is good that we got weekly exercises in JAVA. I think we shouldn't have given the semester project at the beginning of the course where most of us didn't know much about JAVA and OOP concepts. And regarding the semester project it some in